Z||000000||2xsess||09-17-2000||04:40 AM||||Help me please!! My guage lights are extremely dim,I removed all the bulbs and wiped them off with windex. Is it possible that the rotary dimmer is going bad?<P>The lights on the Radio and heater controls are fine though. <P>Thanks,<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||ur2biteme||09-17-2000||07:54 AM||||it's possible.  i have the 85 g.t. gagues in my 87 coupe, and mine arent that dim, but i know the bulbs are a little old (kind of dark on the glass on a few of them, but not blown when i put the cluster in).  i also know that the dimmer wheel is aging too.  i had that problem with my old cluster as well, but all the interior lights got dim.  that was easy to figure out the culprit but hard to fix (alternator)<P>good luck<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>169k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
